P2.10: unify host-path mapping onto core/hostpath; route nginx/certs/cron through it

Three parallel host-path implementations had drifted apart. Consolidated onto
app.core.hostpath as the single source of truth:

- hostpath.to_real() is now the canonical REAL-path mapper (public), and
  handles the HOST_ROOT-itself -> "/" case. _to_real kept as an internal alias.
- project_detector reads HOST_ROOT from hostpath (one env read) and its Path
  _to_real() delegates to hostpath.to_real() — same semantics, no drift. The
  name is still exported for compose.py.
- storage.py imports HOST_ROOT from hostpath instead of re-reading the env.

The nginx/certs/cron scanners previously read /etc/nginx, /etc/letsencrypt and
/etc/cron* DIRECTLY, so in a container (/:/host:ro) they saw the container's
own empty /etc, not the host's. Routed each through hostpath so a dockerized
scan reads the real host configs via /host and reports REAL host paths:

- nginx: scans hostpath.host_glob() of sites-enabled/conf.d; presence of config
  files (not a local nginx binary) gates the scan; certs read via to_read_path.
- certs: lineage listing + cert reads go through the /host mount, with the
  native ls/openssl + sudo -n fallback preserved for root-only native installs.
- cron: /etc/crontab, /etc/cron.d, spool, and periodic dirs read via
  read_host_configs/host_glob; periodic-dir commands report the real host path.

Native behavior (HOST_ROOT unset) is unchanged: host_glob/to_read_path are
no-ops, so all mapping collapses to the original direct reads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
